BEGIN_HYPERDESC
<h1>Test: Earth from 1.35 radii</h1>
<p>A fixed external camera on Earth, for comparing renders between builds and
settings. Nothing here depends on key input or on how long the session has been
running, so two runs are directly comparable pixel for pixel.</p>
<p>Camera::Read (Src/Orbiter/Camera.cpp:1438) takes POS as
&lt;rdist&gt; &lt;phi&gt; &lt;theta&gt; with rdist in units of the TARGET'S RADIUS
(Camera.cpp:134), so 1.35 is about 8600 km from Earth's centre -- the distance
at which the projected terrain shadow map artefact fills the disc.</p>
END_HYPERDESC

BEGIN_ENVIRONMENT
  System Sol
  Date MJD 51982.5292925579
END_ENVIRONMENT

BEGIN_FOCUS
  Ship GL-01
END_FOCUS

BEGIN_CAMERA
  TARGET Earth
  MODE Extern
  POS 3.00 0.00 0.00
  TRACKMODE GlobalFrame
  FOV 50.00
END_CAMERA

BEGIN_HUD
  TYPE Surface
END_HUD

BEGIN_MFD Left
  TYPE Orbit
  PROJ Ship
  REF Earth
END_MFD

BEGIN_MFD Right
  TYPE Surface
END_MFD

BEGIN_SHIPS
GL-01:DeltaGlider
  STATUS Orbiting Earth
  RPOS 3626158.96 4307928.18 -3325004.36
  RVEL 6623.108 -3432.497 2656.884
  AROT -52.67 -56.93 90.32
  PRPLEVEL 0:0.553 1:0.9
  NOSECONE 0 0.0000
  GEAR 0 0.0000
  AIRLOCK 0 0.0000
END
END_SHIPS
